# text = Hareton was impressed with a wholesome terror of encountering either his wild beast's fondness or his madman's rage ; for in one he ran a chance of being squeezed and kissed to death , and in the other of being flung into the fire , or dashed against the wall ; and the poor thing remained perfectly quiet wherever I chose to put him cried Hindley , pulling me back by the skin of my neck , like a dog I answered he said He held the knife in his hand , and pushed its point between my teeth : but , for my part , I was never much afraid of his vagaries .
