# text = A minute previously she was violent ; now , supported on one arm , and not noticing my refusal to obey her , she seemed to find childish diversion in pulling the feathers from the rents she had just made , and ranging them on the sheet according to their different species : her mind had strayed to other associations she murmured to herself I interrupted , dragging the pillow away , and turning the holes towards the mattress , for she was removing its contents by handfuls I went here and there collecting it she continued dreamily I asked she replied said I , resuming my seat , and looping up the curtain that I might watch her she inquired , gazing earnestly at the mirror .
