# text = And now he stared at her so earnestly that I thought the very intensity of his gaze would bring tears into his eyes ; but they burned with anguish : they did not melt said Catherine , leaning back , and returning his look with a suddenly clouded brow : her humour was a mere vane for constantly varying caprices Heathcliff had knelt on one knee to embrace her ; he attempted to rise , but she seized his hair , and kept him down she continued , bitterly cried he , wrenching his head free , and grinding his teeth .
