# text = There seldom passed much talk between them : Linton learnt his lessons and spent his evenings in a small apartment they called the parlour : or else lay in bed all day : for he was constantly getting coughs , and colds , and aches , and pains of some sort added the woman I divined , from this account , that utter lack of sympathy had rendered young Heathcliff selfish and disagreeable , if he were not so originally ; and my interest in him , consequently , decayed : though still I was moved with a sense of grief at his lot , and a wish that he had been left with us .
