# text = After exchanging numerous marks of fondness with him , his cousin went to Mr . Heathcliff , who lingered by the door , dividing his attention between the objects inside and those that lay without : pretending , that is , to observe the latter , and really noting the former alone she cried , reaching up to salute him he answered exclaimed Catherine , flying to attack me next with her lavish caresses replied the uncle , with a hardly suppressed grimace , resulting from his deep aversion to both the proposed visitors he continued , turning towards the young lady asked Catherine , considerably crestfallen answered Heathcliff said the young lady murmured her cousin
