# text = Linton complied ; and had he been unrestrained , would probably have spoiled all by filling his epistles with complaints and lamentations . but his father kept a sharp watch over him ; and , of course , insisted on every line that my master sent being shown ; so , instead of penning his peculiar personal sufferings and distresses , the themes constantly uppermost in his thoughts , he harped on the cruel obligation of being held asunder from his friend and love ; and gently intimated that Mr . Linton must allow an interview soon , or he should fear he was purposely deceiving him with empty promises .
