# text = He glanced fearfully towards the Heights , begging she would remain another half-hour , at least said Cathy he replied observed my young lady , wondering at his pertinacious assertion of what was evidently an untruth continued he , shunning her puzzled gaze exclaimed Cathy , imagining she would be its object said her cousin , shuddering I inquired Linton looked at me , but did not answer ; and , after keeping her seat by his side another ten minutes , during which his head fell drowsily on his breast , and he uttered nothing except suppressed moans of exhaustion or pain , Cathy began to seek solace in looking for bilberries , and sharing the produce of her researches with me : she did not offer them to him , for she saw further notice would only weary and annoy she whispered in my ear , at last I answered returned Catherine I said she answered I remarked Linton here started from his slumber in bewildered terror , and asked if any one had called his name said Catherine he gasped , glancing up to the frowning nab above us replied his cousin
