# text = He didn't cast a glance towards my companions , though they were sufficiently near for Linton's sobs to be audible ; but hailing me in the almost hearty tone he assumed to none besides , and the sincerity of which I couldn't avoid doubting , he said he added , in a lower tone I replied he asked I said he continued , looking at the two young people , who were fixed under his eye - Linton appeared as if he could not venture to stir or raise his head , and Catherine could not move , on his account I answered muttered Heathcliff he shouted Linton had sunk prostrate again in another paroxysm of helpless fear , caused by his father's glance towards him , I suppose : there was nothing else to produce such humiliation .
