# text = I did not mind their skirmishes : but Hareton was often obliged to seek the kitchen also , when the master wanted to have the house to himself ! and though in the beginning she either left it at his approach , or quietly joined in my occupations , and shunned remarking or addressing him - and though he was always as sullen and silent as possible - after a while , she changed her behaviour , and became incapable of letting him alone : talking at him ; commenting on his stupidity and idleness ; expressing her wonder how he could endure the life he lived - how he could sit a whole evening staring into the fire , and dozing she once observed
